{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was that `--out=log.txt` was treated as a single flag name (`out=log.txt`) with value `True`, because the parser never split on `=`.\n\n**Fix:** After stripping `--`, if the remainder contains `=`, split on the first `=` into name and value. Otherwise keep the existing behavior: consume the next token as the value when it isn’t another flag, or set the flag to `True`.\n\nThe loop is also a bit clearer: handle non-flag tokens with an early continue, use `body` for the flag text, and use explicit `continue` paths so each case is obvious.\n\n`old_parse_flags` is unchanged in behavior; only the inline TODO was turned into a short docstring.\n\nBoth tests in `tests/visible/test_flags.py` pass."}]},"session_id":"563c41ef-d2f7-4c72-90cf-be657cdbff82"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":70585,"duration_api_ms":70585,"is_error":false,"result":"Inspecting `repo/cli.py` and how arguments are parsed.\n\n\nFixing `--key=value` parsing and clarifying the parser logic.\n\n\nThe problem was that `--out=log.txt` was treated as a single flag name (`out=log.txt`) with value `True`, because the parser never split on `=`.\n\n**Fix:** After stripping `--`, if the remainder contains `=`, split on the first `=` into name and value. Otherwise keep the existing behavior: consume the next token as the value when it isn’t another flag, or set the flag to `True`.\n\nThe loop is also a bit clearer: handle non-flag tokens with an early continue, use `body` for the flag text, and use explicit `continue` paths so each case is obvious.\n\n`old_parse_flags` is unchanged in behavior; only the inline TODO was turned into a short docstring.\n\nBoth tests in `tests/visible/test_flags.py` pass.","session_id":"563c41ef-d2f7-4c72-90cf-be657cdbff82","request_id":"074f350f-07ed-430a-bb17-27f30eb2e64c","usage":{"inputTokens":12734,"outputTokens":1800,"cacheReadTokens":78412,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
